:name: P0 Blinky
:description: Boots the P0 firmware on the STM32H743 platform (plus the project overlay).

# Overridable from Robot / CLI:  renode -e '$bin=@...' pN.resc
$name?="p0_blinky"
$bin?=@build/fw/p0_blinky/p0_blinky.elf
$plant_port?=4321

using sysbus
mach create $name

machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/stm32h743.repl
# Project overlay: fixes and additions on top of the upstream platform (create when needed)
# machine LoadPlatformDescription @projects/p0_blinky/renode/p0_overlay.repl

# Logs/console: ST-LINK VCP = USART3
# Plant link (P1+): socket terminal bridged to the Python co-sim bridge
# emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal $plant_port "plant" false
# connector Connect sysbus.usart2 plant

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
"""
runMacro $reset

# GUI conveniences live in p0_gui.resc (which does `include @.../p0.resc` then
# `showAnalyzer sysbus.usart3`), because .resc has no conditionals and this file must stay headless.
